From 690152411dae2c8a5d261d866f1f0f963ab02324 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: qwen38-4090 <noreply@localhost>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 00:20:52 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 02/49] Ada: two-stage small-T schedules, dual-grid paired
 input projections

Measured with weights rotated past the 72 MB L2 (kernels/bench_ada.cu, bench_dual.cu):
- every retuned schedule keeps Warps = 8, so accumulation order and bits are unchanged;
  two pipeline stages beat three on every shape.
- T in [7,16]: GDN qk and attention q/k (Q4) leave the Q4 K-split kernel for the Ada small-T
  kernel, in one grid with their Q5 partner. GDN input 72.5 -> 57.4 us, attention input
  70.1 -> 50.0 us at T=16.
End to end (DFlash2-15 verify tree, K8V4): json 282 -> 311, code 347 -> 375, prose 131 -> 149,
sustained 239 -> 262 tok/s.
